course: dictionary
lesson: 2636
title: Destroy: ruin or end
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To destroy something means to damage it so badly that it is ruined or no longer exists. The clues around the word tell you what happened. In the harvest mouse sentence, «harvesting machines can destroy those nests», the machines damage the nests, so destroy means ruin. Swap in your meaning and check: «harvesting machines can ruin those nests» still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Look at the clues before the word. In «The fire destroyed the old barn», the words «the fire» show what caused the damage. In «An old idea that invaders destroyed the Indus cities suddenly is now not believed», the word «suddenly» is a clue: the idea is that the cities were destroyed in one sudden moment, and experts now think the change was slow.
explain: Destroy can have other meanings too. In a game, «We destroyed them at football» is informal and means we beat them completely. When someone's hopes or plans are destroyed, they come to an end. The clues tell you which meaning fits: a game means beat, and hopes or plans mean end.
fact: Destroy is a verb: destroy, destroys, destroyed, destroying.
fact: To destroy something means to damage it so badly that it is ruined or no longer exists.
fact: «Destroyed by fire» means the fire ruined it completely.
fact: To destroy someone's hopes or plans means to end them.
fact: People safely destroy old papers with personal information, so no one else can read them.
exercise: «The harvest mouse weaves a ball-shaped nest among tall grass.» Harvesting machines can destroy those nests. What does destroy mean? | Count | *Ruin, so the nests are no longer there | Move gently | Build
exercise: Sam says, «We destroyed them at football!» What does destroy mean here? | Cleaned the pitch | Built a wall around them | *Beat them completely | Ran away from them
exercise: «The storm destroyed the old barn.» Find and copy the word that shows what the storm did. | old | storm | barn | *destroyed
test: «The flood destroyed the bridge, so the road was closed.» What does destroyed mean? | Built | Painted | Cleaned | *Ruined, so it was no longer there
test: Mia says, «The rain destroyed our plans for a day at the beach.» What does destroyed mean here? | Made them bigger | Made them come true | *Ended, so the plans could not happen | Sang about them
exam: Why do people safely destroy old papers with personal information? | So you can forget what they say | *So no one else can read your private details | So the papers get longer | So the papers can be read aloud
